Core Chest CT Acquisition Principles

Spiral / Helical CT
Continuous acquisition while patient moves through gantry
Entire chest acquired in a single breath-hold

Reduces:
motion artifact
misregistration
skip areas

Enables:
CT angiography
multiplanar reconstructions
overlapping thin slices 

Multidetector CT (MDCT)
Modern scanners use 256 to 320 detector rows
Allows contiguous thin-section acquisition of the entire thorax
1 mm isotropic voxels enable:
sagittal/coronal reformats
3D reconstructions
virtual bronchoscopy
CT angiography 

Standard Chest CT Protocol
Indications
Pulmonary nodules
